     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\">You set equality constraints by using the same label for different model coefficients. For example, in your syntax, you might do this:</div><p style=\"font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Menlo;color:rgb(202,51,35)\"><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">model15 </span><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures;color:rgb(209,113,37)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures\">&#39;F1 =~ NA*var1 + var2</span></p><p style=\"font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Menlo;color:rgb(202,51,35)\"><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures\">             F2 =~ NA*var3 </span></p><p style=\"font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Menlo;color:rgb(202,51,35)\"><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures\">             F3 =~ NA*var4 + var5         </span></p><p style=\"font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Menlo;color:rgb(202,51,35)\"><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures\">             F1~~a*F3</span></p><p style=\"font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Menlo;color:rgb(202,51,35)\"><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures\">             F1~~a*F2</span></p><p style=\"font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Menlo;color:rgb(202,51,35)\"><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures\">             F2~~F3</span></p><p style=\"font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Menlo;color:rgb(202,51,35)\"><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures\">             var3 ~~ 0*var3&#39;</span></p><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div class=\"gmail_attr\">However, your model will still be not identified unless you eitehr fix factor variances or constrain some loadings.</div><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\"><br></div><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Thu, Aug 27, 2020 at 11:17 AM Sarah Colbert &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">saco...@colorado.edu</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi All, <div><br></div><div>I have just started using lavaan for an SEM project and have a quick question. This is the model I am currently working with: </div><div><br></div><div><p style=\"font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Menlo;color:rgb(202,51,35)\"><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">model15 </span><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures;color:rgb(209,113,37)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures\">&#39;F1 =~ NA*var1 + var2</span></p><p style=\"font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Menlo;color:rgb(202,51,35)\"><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures\"><span>             </span>F2 =~ NA*var3<span> </span></span></p><p style=\"font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Menlo;color:rgb(202,51,35)\"><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures\"><span>             </span>F3 =~ NA*var4 + var5<span>         </span></span></p><p style=\"font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Menlo;color:rgb(202,51,35)\"><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures\"><span>             </span>F1~~F3</span></p><p style=\"font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Menlo;color:rgb(202,51,35)\"><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures\"><span>             </span>F1~~F2</span></p><p style=\"font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Menlo;color:rgb(202,51,35)\"><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures\"><span>             </span>F2~~F3</span></p><p style=\"font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Menlo;color:rgb(202,51,35)\"><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures\"><span>             var3</span> ~~ 0*var3&#39;</span></p><p style=\"font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Menlo;color:rgb(202,51,35)\"><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures\"><br></span></p><p style=\"font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Menlo;color:rgb(202,51,35)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">I would like to add a constraint so that the correlation between F1 and F3 is equal to the correlation between F1 and F2. I have tried using F1~~F3 == F1~~F2, however that did not work. </span><br></p><p style=\"font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Menlo;color:rgb(202,51,35)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><br></span></p><p style=\"font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Menlo;color:rgb(202,51,35)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">I read the section on equality constraints on the lavaan tutorial page but I&#39;m not sure how to apply the code to my model. Any help would be greatly appreciated!</span></p><p style=\"font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Menlo;color:rgb(202,51,35)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><br></span></p><p style=\"font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Menlo;color:rgb(202,51,35)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Thanks,</span></p><p style=\"font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Menlo;color:rgb(202,51,35)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><br></span></p><p style=\"font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Menlo;color:rgb(202,51,35)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Sarah</span></p></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;lavaan&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">lavaan+un...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r